data.content:
✅ **Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers.** Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work with `stackalloc`:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, `nint.Size` is 8 bytes. The feature has been available since C# 9 / .NET 5 when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced as first-class unmanaged types (which is the requirement for `stackalloc`).
